%% HANDWRITTEN. Checked against ARCHITECTURE.md S8 + D22 + D23 + D38
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant Q as Waiting pool
    participant M as MatchingEngine
    participant PR as Presence
    participant SOLV as Hungarian solver
    participant WS as Agent workstation

    Note over Q,WS: ONE pool - not one queue per agent (D22)

    loop every tick, and on every relevant event
        M->>Q: all waiting calls
        M->>PR: all offerable agents
        Note right of PR: two axes: what the PLATFORM knows,<br/>and what the PERSON chose (D33)

        M->>M: hard filters FIRST
        Note right of M: required skill - LANGUAGE (D38)<br/>a failed hard filter is not a low score,<br/>it is exclusion

        M->>M: fit score for every (call, agent) pair
        Note right of M: skill_match + continuity +<br/>historical_fit - load_penalty

        M->>M: urgency multiplier per call
        Note right of M: wait_pressure + sla_risk + customer_priority<br/>+ situational. This is what stops starvation.

        M->>SOLV: cost matrix
        SOLV-->>M: globally optimal assignment
        Note right of SOLV: greedy best-first is locally optimal<br/>and globally poor - it strands people

        alt a much better agent frees up in seconds
            M->>M: DEFER, but only inside the guard rails
            Note right of M: never past the wait ceiling,<br/>never for a critical call
        else
            M->>WS: OFFER
            Note right of WS: every candidate and its score is persisted -<br/>the decision is explainable (D18)
        end
    end
